1
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:51,790
Come on! You're almost there!

2
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:53,520
Keep it up!

3
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,130
Nine hours, 12 minutes.

4
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,660
Not bad given the conditions
you had to trudge through.

5
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,060
[EREN sighs]

6
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,530
Thought we were
dead out there.

7
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:06,340
Dammit. Nobody said training
was gonna be this rough.

8
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:08,810
Anyone else
not feel their legs?

9
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:11,480
Why won't they
let us inside already?

10
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:13,180
[SASHA] I bet they're busy
laying out a massive

11
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:15,610
banquet for us as we speak.

12
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:18,880
[REINER] Hey!
You guys seen Christa?

13
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,180
[EREN]
Huh?

14
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:22,320
Not for a while.
She was with Daz,

15
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:24,290
and he wasn't doing so good.

16
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:25,890
Yeah, well he's not here.

17
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:28,130
Ymir isn't back yet either.

18
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:30,460
[MARCO] They're probably
mixed in with the last squad.

19
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,460
[REINER] That's just it.
Thomas was leading

20
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:35,830
the last squad.
Says they never saw them.

21
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:37,840
[All gasp]

22
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:43,510
Whoa, hold on.
Do you think they're lost?

23
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:44,910
Ooof. Man, if they
get stuck out there

24
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:47,280
in this snowstorm,
they're done for.

25
00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:48,650
Son of a--!

26
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:50,710
Eren!

27
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:53,280
I have to go back out there
and try to find 'em!

28
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,620
[MARCO]
I'm with you!

29
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:56,550
[FEMALE INSTRUCTOR 30A]
In the cabin. Now.

30
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:57,750
[EREN]
But, Christa and--

31
00:02:57,790 --> 00:03:01,130
We know. A rescue team will
be sent out at first light.

32
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,760
They'll have frozen
to death by then!

33
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,300
Do you want
more people to die?

34
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:15,770
Dammit.

35
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:32,260
[YMIR]
Christa.

36
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:35,860
Seriously, give it up.
This is pointless.

37
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:41,430
No it's not.

38
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:44,900
[YMIR] Dumb bastard's got one
foot in the grave as it is.

39
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:47,670
Nobody to blame but
himself if you ask me.

40
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:49,270
Should've known
how much he could handle

41
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:51,780
before trying
to boost his score.

42
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:55,680
Some people just aren't
cut out to be soldiers.

43
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:57,510
He'll be long gone
by the time you make it

44
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:59,680
to the foot of that mountain.

45
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,220
Rate we're going, we'll be
lucky not to join him.

46
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:04,290
It's a zero sum game.

47
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:07,460
Way I see it,
we've got two choices.

48
00:04:07,490 --> 00:04:10,730
Leave Daz to the elements
and save our own skin,

49
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,860
or die a cozy little trio.

50
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:15,700
What's it gonna be?

51
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:17,430
You left one out.

52
00:04:17,470 --> 00:04:19,570
Third option:
you're completely wrong.

53
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:21,870
I reach base in plenty
of time to save his life

54
00:04:21,910 --> 00:04:25,380
and by morning this is
all a bad memory.

55
00:04:25,410 --> 00:04:27,980
There's no reason
for you to stick with me.

56
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:30,610
We'll only slow you down.

57
00:04:30,650 --> 00:04:33,350
You'll make it back
a lot faster on your own.

58
00:04:33,390 --> 00:04:35,520
Daz and I'll be
right behind you.

59
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:37,790
Go on ahead.

60
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:46,260
[CHRISTA gasps]

61
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:55,440
So, uh...
You got something against

62
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:58,940
asking me for help or what?

63
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:01,910
Know what I think?
I think saving this moron

64
00:05:01,950 --> 00:05:04,980
is the furthest thing
from your mind.

65
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,960
[YMIR] You're not
worried about Daz.

66
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:23,670
You're just using him
as an excuse to die.

67
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:27,870
This is how you want
your story to end. Right?

68
00:05:27,910 --> 00:05:31,540
What a shame. Here I thought
you were the good girl.

69
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:33,080
Of course, if you can
make it look like you were

70
00:05:33,110 --> 00:05:35,950
trying to save his life,
no one will be the wiser.

71
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,950
Hey. They'll remember
you as a hero

72
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,480
who fearlessly
sacrificed herself.

73
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,890
He's a small
price to pay, right?

74
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,960
If you're a selfish bitch.

75
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:47,860
[CHRISTA gasps]
That's not--!

76
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:52,530
I never meant--
That's not me.

77
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:58,640
[CHRISTA]
It's just...

78
00:06:00,070 --> 00:06:01,710
I know you.

79
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:05,710
You're the mistress' daughter
with the price on her head.

80
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,410
How could you possibly?

81
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:13,050
[YMIR] Uh-huh.
There go any doubts I had.

82
00:06:13,090 --> 00:06:14,920
Let's just say
I have a knack for being

83
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:17,650
in the wrong place
at the right time.

84
00:06:17,690 --> 00:06:20,460
Snuck inside a church
in the interior once

85
00:06:20,490 --> 00:06:21,860
scrounging around
for whatever might

86
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:24,800
keep me alive another week.

87
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:27,460
Quite a story
I got treated to.

88
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,830
Apparently a high-ranking
noble produced more heirs

89
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,700
than his people
were comfortable with.

90
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,540
An illegitimate girl
was floating around

91
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:35,540
they all feared might
come out of nowhere one day

92
00:06:35,570 --> 00:06:37,670
and claim a share
in his legacy.

93
00:06:37,710 --> 00:06:38,910
Some wanted her dead,

94
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,780
some wanted to strip her
of the family name

95
00:06:40,810 --> 00:06:42,950
and hide her
among peasant stock.

96
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:45,150
In the end, clever
bastards forced her

97
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:47,420
to join the Cadet Corps.

98
00:06:49,150 --> 00:06:50,820
Don't worry, sweetheart.

99
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:52,890
Your true identity
is safe with me.

100
00:06:52,930 --> 00:06:55,860
I haven't told a soul
and I don't plan to.

101
00:06:55,890 --> 00:06:58,830
So was, was your
whole reason for joining

102
00:06:58,860 --> 00:07:01,400
the Cadet Corps
just to find me?

103
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:04,430
Why would you even care?

104
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:06,770
[YMIR inhales]

105
00:07:06,810 --> 00:07:09,910
I dunno. Maybe I relate
to your struggle.

106
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:11,840
[CHRISTA gasps]

107
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:15,950
So we... have more
in common than I thought?

108
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:19,680
Well, uh.
You could say that.

109
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:22,420
I'm why you're...
a soldier?

110
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:25,390
Could be.
I'm not positive.

111
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:28,760
Uh, actually, no.

112
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:30,760
So why, then?

113
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:33,400
Did you want us
to become friends?

114
00:07:33,430 --> 00:07:37,430
Ha! You have
got to be joking.

115
00:07:38,870 --> 00:07:41,740
[YMIR] The only thing we have
in common is a second chance.

116
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:44,710
Look, don't try to read
anything else into it, okay?

117
00:07:44,740 --> 00:07:47,880
Unlike you, I embraced
the name I was born with.

118
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:51,750
If I throw it away and reject
who I am, then they win.

119
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:53,620
I intend to live my life.

120
00:07:53,650 --> 00:07:55,990
Make my name mean something.

121
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:58,160
Trust me, there's no
revenge in the world

122
00:07:58,190 --> 00:08:00,960
sweeter than that.
Look at yourself, Christa--

123
00:08:00,990 --> 00:08:02,390
or whoever you are.

124
00:08:02,430 --> 00:08:03,860
You've been a victim
all your life,

125
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,530
and how do you
get your revenge?

126
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:07,630
By becoming your own victim!

127
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:10,030
Screw you and this
stupid death wish!

128
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:15,110
If you kill yourself, you'll be
doing exactly what they want!

129
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:19,680
I-- That's not how--
I just--

130
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:23,210
I didn't mean
to get us into this

131
00:08:23,250 --> 00:08:26,180
and now there's
nothing we can do.

132
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:28,080
[YMIR]
Bullshit.

133
00:08:36,930 --> 00:08:40,230
The base is a
straight drop from here.

134
00:08:42,670 --> 00:08:44,900
[YMIR] I say we
dump him off the cliff.

135
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,540
[CHRISTA gasps]

136
00:08:46,610 --> 00:08:48,240
It's possible
he'll survive the fall.

137
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:50,740
If they find him
then he might be okay.

138
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,040
Sure, it's a long shot,

139
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:54,910
but that's what
we're dealing with.

140
00:08:54,950 --> 00:08:57,050
Unless we're
due for a miracle,

141
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,950
even if you live
to drag him down there

142
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:00,920
all you'll have in tow
by the time you make it

143
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:02,520
is a frozen corpse.

144
00:09:02,550 --> 00:09:06,960
But, if he falls
he'll die for certain!

145
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:08,960
Enough of this shit!

146
00:09:08,990 --> 00:09:11,560
[CHRISTA] What are
you doing? Put me down!

147
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:13,600
I'll handle Daz,
you get moving!

148
00:09:13,630 --> 00:09:15,730
[CHRISTA yells]

149
00:09:15,770 --> 00:09:18,030
[Grunts]

150
00:09:22,910 --> 00:09:25,610
[Distant rumble]

151
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:35,820
[CHRISTA gasps and panting]

152
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,760
[CHRISTA]
No.

153
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:41,730
Ymir!

154
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:44,630
Wait! Please!

155
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:53,000
What's going on?

156
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:54,840
Where did they--?

157
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:59,940
[EREN] It's better if you guys
let me do this alone.

158
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:01,710
Like our instructors said--

159
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:04,650
We don't want more people
to die than may already have.

160
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,950
That's precisely why
I'm coming with you.

161
00:10:06,990 --> 00:10:09,720
I can't just sit around
here and do nothing.

162
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:13,220
[REINER] Really?
What the hell is this?

163
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:15,030
[EREN] Look,
don't try to stop me!

164
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:18,860
You're, uh, gonna need
a lot more gear.

165
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,600
You can't do this
on your own.

166
00:10:20,630 --> 00:10:22,970
You'll end up just like the
folks you're trying to rescue.

167
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,700
The more eyes you've got
in your search party,

168
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:26,140
the better, right?

169
00:10:26,170 --> 00:10:28,200
Well, we--

170
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:31,640
I suppose we could use
all the help we can get.

171
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:34,810
[CONNY] Great.
Then count us in, too.

172
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:37,150
Sounds like the storm's
letting up a little bit.

173
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,720
We should be okay.

174
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:40,620
I brought some extra
rations just in case!

175
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:41,720
Thanks, guys.

176
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:47,720
[Distant rumble]

177
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:50,760
What was that?
An avalanche?

178
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:01,170
Look, somebody's coming!

179
00:11:08,850 --> 00:11:16,690
[CHRISTA breathes laboringly]

180
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,720
Ymir?

181
00:11:20,290 --> 00:11:21,830
It's about time.

182
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:23,990
You decide to take
the scenic route?

183
00:11:24,030 --> 00:11:25,930
I told Reiner and the gang
I'd wait out here

184
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:29,970
to be your welcoming
committee, so--

185
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,040
Yeah, I know.
Stupid move on my part.

186
00:11:33,070 --> 00:11:35,040
Daz! Is he--?

187
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:50,720
[CHRISTA] From all
the way up there?

188
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,160
But you didn't have
any rope on you.

189
00:11:53,190 --> 00:11:56,290
And even if you did, how?

190
00:11:56,330 --> 00:11:59,330
It would've taken
hours to repel down!

191
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:04,970
Yeah, all right.

192
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,270
If I have to trust someone,
then it might as well be you.

193
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:12,140
Just... gimme your word.

194
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:14,040
When the day comes
for me to reveal myself

195
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:17,180
to everyone, promise.

196
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:20,780
Promise to take back your
name and live your life.

197
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,850
[Gasps]

198
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:37,430
[CHRISTA]
Ymir!

199
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:41,340
[YMIR]
Christa. We're the same.

200
00:12:41,370 --> 00:12:45,310
I used to curse the day
I was born, just like you.

201
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:49,380
The world despised me
for having the gall to exist.

202
00:12:49,410 --> 00:12:52,020
Heh. I thought the only
way to put things right

203
00:12:52,050 --> 00:12:55,420
was to give up my life.

204
00:12:55,450 --> 00:12:57,720
But even then,
what I wished for

205
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,960
more than anything...

206
00:12:59,990 --> 00:13:02,890
...was to be given
a second chance.

207
00:13:02,930 --> 00:13:07,500
A chance to finally
live for myself!

208
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:12,000
[Roars]

209
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:26,550
[Roars]

210
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:33,220
[CONNY] Talk to me. Somebody
tell me it's all a dream.

211
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:35,150
Ymir.

212
00:13:35,190 --> 00:13:38,820
[Gasps]
It was her that day.

213
00:13:44,970 --> 00:13:46,870
She's the one.

214
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:58,280
[Screams]

215
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:05,080
Thank you, Reiner. I--

216
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,020
[Yelps]

217
00:14:06,050 --> 00:14:08,090
Stop, you're hurting me!

218
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:10,390
[CONNY]
Hey! Take it easy, man!

219
00:14:10,460 --> 00:14:15,030
That's enough! Let go! Let go!

220
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,200
I'm so sorry!

221
00:14:18,230 --> 00:14:19,400
It's okay.

222
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:20,570
Tell me the truth.

223
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:23,940
You had to have been
in on all this.

224
00:14:23,970 --> 00:14:28,570
Ymir's a Titan.
How could you not know?

225
00:14:28,610 --> 00:14:31,240
She never told me.

226
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:33,510
We were inseparable.

227
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:37,280
And yet, I had no idea.

228
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,090
I mean, how?

229
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:44,160
[Roars]

230
00:14:44,190 --> 00:14:45,960
Not sure what to think.

231
00:14:45,990 --> 00:14:48,660
All this time she's been
keeping it under wraps

232
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:51,460
and we never suspected
a damn thing.

233
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,100
Yeah.

234
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:57,000
Well, it's possible
she didn't know.

235
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,000
Eren was caught off guard.

236
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,870
He had no clue
till he transformed.

237
00:15:01,910 --> 00:15:05,510
Then again, Ymir did
seem to have a plan.

238
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:08,950
Wait a second;
are you trying to say that

239
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:10,380
Ymir is a threat?

240
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:13,590
Maybe. It's a hell of
a power to hide.

241
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:17,320
How she'll use it
is anybody's guess.

242
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:18,920
For all we know
she could've been

243
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,490
on their side all along.

244
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:26,400
[Roars]

245
00:15:26,430 --> 00:15:28,300
[CHRISTA gasps]

246
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:32,340
[CHRISTA]
Ymir!

247
00:15:56,100 --> 00:15:58,560
Whoa! What is she doing?

248
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,330
[Roars]

249
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:03,370
Oh, come on!
You're kidding, right?

250
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:06,240
She's worried about
the tower falling down?

251
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:09,340
Exactly. She didn't
have to stay.

252
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,510
She could've chosen to escape.

253
00:16:11,550 --> 00:16:13,510
Nothing's keeping her here.

254
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:18,580
And still...
She's fighting.

255
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:22,690
It's us. She's risking
her life for us!

256
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:29,630
Who are you?

257
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:33,730
Why are you
doing this? Why?

258
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:37,440
Don't you die on me!

259
00:16:37,470 --> 00:16:39,710
Not in a hovel
like this, damn you!

260
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:40,810
Whoa!

261
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:44,780
[CHRISTA] You want to be
the hero all of a sudden?

262
00:16:44,810 --> 00:16:47,550
Ha! Hoping to go out
in a blaze of glory?

263
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,280
Don't make me laugh!

264
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,420
Too late to
think about heaven now!

265
00:16:51,450 --> 00:16:54,590
You're a selfish bitch
and you know it!

266
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:57,020
You'll die protecting
this stupid tower!

267
00:16:57,060 --> 00:16:59,960
Tear it to pieces!
Live for yourself!

268
00:16:59,990 --> 00:17:01,560
[CONNY]
Christa!

269
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:12,640
[Intense music plays]

270
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:17,340
Shit! Brace yourselves,
people. This is happening!

271
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:19,540
Yeah! Atta girl!

272
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:27,190
Wanna live? Grab on tight.

273
00:17:44,370 --> 00:17:48,040
[Rumble]

274
00:17:54,010 --> 00:17:55,750
[Coughs]

275
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,490
[Both gasp]

276
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:04,690
They're still not dead?

277
00:18:04,730 --> 00:18:08,360
Hey, ugly! You've got
a job to finish!

278
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:16,470
Ymir!

279
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:19,300
[TITAN YMIR panting]

280
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:25,280
That's not good.

281
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:28,650
[TITANS roar]

282
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:39,620
[Squelching]

283
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:43,230
They're eating her!

284
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:46,830
[CHRISTA]
No. No, please.

285
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:50,740
Christa, wait!

286
00:18:50,770 --> 00:18:55,070
[CHRISTA]
Ymir! Don't do this to me!

287
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:59,480
Damn it! We had
a deal, remember?

288
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:03,520
Hold on! I still haven't
told you my name!

289
00:19:03,550 --> 00:19:06,890
I promised you!

290
00:19:18,370 --> 00:19:21,830
[CHRISTA]
No! I still haven't...

291
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:36,280
[MIKASA] Christa,
all of you, get back.

292
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:39,890
It's okay. Let us
take care of this.

293
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,520
Mikasa!

294
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:44,260
[ALL gasp]

295
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:51,260
[HANGE] Disperse and
canvas the area!

296
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:52,500
The rest of you
follow me to where

297
00:19:52,530 --> 00:19:54,530
the Titans are gathering
and cut them down!

298
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:56,430
Got it!

299
00:19:56,470 --> 00:20:00,140
Wait! You're not
part of the offensive!

300
00:20:02,310 --> 00:20:04,710
Die!

301
00:20:04,750 --> 00:20:07,750
Ha-ha!
My very first ODM kill!

302
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:12,520
[EREN hollers]

303
00:20:12,550 --> 00:20:15,250
[KEIJI] Idiot!
I told you to fall back!

304
00:20:15,290 --> 00:20:17,220
Right! I'm sorry, sir!

305
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,920
Ow, damn.

306
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:22,590
[CONNY]
Hey! Eren!

307
00:20:22,630 --> 00:20:24,600
We found 'em!

308
00:20:40,550 --> 00:20:42,580
[Yells]

309
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:17,950
Can't be. She's really...?

310
00:21:22,790 --> 00:21:25,590
[CHRISTA]
Ymir.

311
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:41,070
Just as promised.

312
00:21:41,110 --> 00:21:44,910
My real name is Historia.

313
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:14,910
♪ Closing Song
